.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# data/projects.json, data/programs.json, data/system_config.json, and
# data/plugins/core/*.json used to be intentionally NOT ignored (tracked in
# this repo so everyone got them via git pull / Update and Restart), but
# that meant any machine with an uncommitted local edit broke the
# self-update git pull outright. They're now synced via Google Cloud
# Storage instead (core/cloud_sync.py) — each is a local cache of the
# shared bucket's blob, pulled on launch and pushed on every save, so they
# no longer belong in git at all. data/thumbnails/ (and the other image
# dirs) are unaffected — still git-tracked as before. Every per-machine/
# gitignored file (local_config.json, github_token.json,
# gcs_refresh_token.json, webengine_profile/, plugin_local_config/) lives
# under /cache/ instead, not data/ — see that rule below and
# cache/README.md.
data/projects.json
data/programs.json
data/system_config.json
data/plugins/core/*.json
.pytest_cache/
# plugins/core and plugins/repo_internal are both git-tracked and
# distributed like data/programs.json — bundled with the app, no separate
# fetch. See core/extensibility/loader.py.
# Forced workspace_root (see launcher.py) — actual cloned target repos live
# here, per-machine and potentially huge; never tracked.
/projects/
# Every per-machine, gitignored file UkoreHub itself owns lives under here —
# see cache/README.md. Includes cache/plugins/, per-user clones of repo
# plugins (each its own git clone/remote/history, fetched/updated on demand
# for a repo that declares it as a requirement — see plugins/README.md).
/cache/
# PyInstaller intermediates from developer/packaging/build_exe.py —
# regenerate every build, never committed. The resulting UkoreHub.exe at
# the repo root IS committed — a shared studio-wide binary, same pattern as
# data/thumbnails/ and data/programs.json above.
/developer/build/
*.spec
# Old UkoreHub.exe renamed aside by updater.py's _relocate_self_exe during a
# self-update (Windows won't let git overwrite the exe while it's running,
# but it will let it be renamed) — cleaned up automatically on the next
# launch, never committed.
/UkoreHub.exe.old-*
